<<
/Title (Q: What is the primary factor driving the recent divergence between digital assets and traditional equities? A: The primary driver is the shift in internal liquidity plumbing, specifically the contraction in Fed Net Liquidity observed on March 18. While the S&P 500 showed early resilience, digital assets reacted more sensitively to the ~$6 billion liquidity drain and the strengthening DXY, which rebounded above 120.5. This suggests a "risk-off" transition where capital moves toward the dollar as a defensive measure.)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 902 0 R
/Next 1198 0 R
>>
endobj
1107 0 obj
<<
/Title (Q: How should we interpret the $800M BTC inflow on March 21 given the continued price decline toward $82K? A: This anomaly suggests a complex market dynamic. Historically, large inflows to exchanges are associated with selling pressure; however, given the price was already at its weekly low, this could also represent "whale absorption" or a preparation for significant volatility. We must monitor if this inflow leads to a stabilization or if it serves as a precursor to further distribution by large holders.)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 902 0 R
/Prev 1199 0 R
>>
endobj
