/Title (Q: Does the minor uptick in High Yield Credit Spreads signal a broader systemic crisis? A: Not at this stage. Although spreads have moved up toward 3.3%, they remain significantly below the 4.5% "Caution Level" and the 6.0% "Crisis Level". The current movement is a normalization of risk premiums after a period of extreme tightness, suggesting that while market participants are becoming more vigilant, credit markets do not yet price in a high probability of structural default.)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 902 0 R
/Prev 1198 0 R
/Next 1107 0 R
